        "display": "lived",
        "explain": "Statement order (I lived) and backshift; no ‘do’."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“What are you doing?” → She asked what I",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(do)",
        "answers": [
          "was doing"
        ],
        "display": "was doing",
        "explain": "Statement order: subject + was doing."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“When does the film start?” → He asked when the film",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(start)",
        "answers": [
          "started"
        ],
        "display": "started",
        "explain": "No ‘does’; the subject comes first: the film started."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“Why did you leave?” → They asked why I",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(leave)",
        "answers": [
          "had left"
        ],
        "display": "had left",
        "explain": "Past simple moves back to past perfect: had left."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“How old are you?” → She asked how old I",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(be)",
        "answers": [
          "was"
        ],
        "display": "was",
        "explain": "Statement order: how old I was."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“Where is the station?” → A tourist asked me where the station",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(be)",
        "answers": [
          "was"
        ],
        "display": "was",
        "explain": "The verb goes after the subject: the station was."
      },
      {
        "use": "Wh-",
        "before": "“What time is it?” → He asked what time it",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(be)",
        "answers": [
          "was"
        ],
        "display": "was",
        "explain": "Statement order and backshift: it was."
      },
      {
        "use": "Question word",
        "before": "“",
        "after": "broke the window?” → She asked who had broken the window.",
        "hint": "who / what",
        "answers": [
          "Who"
        ],
        "display": "Who",
        "explain": "‘Who’ is the subject here, so the order stays the same."
      },
      {
        "use": "Question word",
        "before": "“What happened?” → He asked what",
        "after": ".",
        "hint": "(happen)",
        "answers": [
          "had happened"
        ],
        "display": "had happened",
        "explain": "‘What’ is the subject: no inversion; past simple → past perfect."
      },
      {
        "use": "Reporting verb",
        "before": "She",
        "after": "me where I had bought my jacket.",
        "hint": "asked / said",
        "answers": [
          "asked"
